# Code owners are requested for review automatically when a pull request
# touches their files. For each file the LAST matching rule wins, so keep
# broad rules above the narrower ones that refine them.
#
# A `## <Area>` heading names the rules below it. The "Suggested reviewers"
# pull request comment (.github/workflows/codeowners-comment.yml) uses it to
# explain why someone was requested, so keep it short and descriptive.
#
# Every file must match some rule (enforced by
# .github/scripts/test_codeowners_comment.py). A rule without owners marks
# files that intentionally have none.

## Unowned: touched by most pull requests, so owning them would ping everyone
